---
import Tooltip from "../../elements/Tooltip.astro";
import AtomSymbol from "../../elements/AtomSymbol.astro";
import Music from "../../elements/Music.astro";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import melancholia from "../../../assets/other/melancholia.png";
import book from "../../../assets/other/book.png";
import life from "../../../assets/other/life.png";
import SubSection from "../../structure/SubSection.astro";

---

<AtomSymbol include_classes="w-20 h-20 mb-10" />
<SubSection
  label="Personal"
  title="Outside of Work"
  show_link={false}
  include_classes="mb-10"
/>
<p>
  I like to watch dark psychological thrillers that are too much to watch more
  than once. Don't ask me why I've watched
  <Tooltip text="Melancholia">
    <span class="inline-block mb-2 text-left"
      >A Danish psychological thriller film written and directed by Lars von
      Trier.</span
    >
    <Image
      src={melancholia}
      alt="Melancholia"
      class="w-[200px]"
      loading="lazy"
    />
  </Tooltip>
  way more than needed. I also enjoy watching soccer, reading the occasional
  <Tooltip text="book">
    <span class="flex items-center gap-2">
      <span class="inline-block mb-2 text-left"
        >Currently reading The Anthropocene Reviewed by John Green.</span
      >
      <Image src={book} alt="Book" class="w-20" loading="lazy" />
    </span>
  </Tooltip>, and playing with my kiddo and crazy dog.
</p>

<figure class="picture-frame">
  <Image src={life} alt="Life" class="w-[790px]" loading="lazy" />
</figure>

<figcaption class="text-left text-sm mt-4">
  <span>Working tirelessly for them.</span>
</figcaption>

<h3>Currently Listening</h3>
<div class="mt-5 mb-10">
  <Music />
</div>

<style>
  .picture-frame {
    @apply flex justify-center w-full bg-theme-surface-light border-[5px] border-white rounded-lg shadow-lg;
  }
</style>
